<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Chilembwe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1871–1915</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Chilembwe was a Baptist minister and educator in Nyasaland, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a>. Educated in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, he founded the Providence Industrial Mission near Chiradzulu, and in January 1915 he led a short-lived rising against the abuses of British planters and colonial rule. He was shot by police while fleeing, and he is honoured in Malawi as a national hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-chilembwe.jpg" alt="John Chilembwe" width="213" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Chilembwe_(2)_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
